<h1>Rimrock & Otter — Site Copy (July 11, 2026)</h1>
<h1>Homepage (index.html)</h1>
<p><b>Meta description:</b> Rimrock & Otter teaches animism and nature-spirit guidance, helping you recognize the signs and life force already around you.</p>
<h2>Hero</h2>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Everything has a spirit you were born to know.</p>
<p>You are wildkind. Rediscover what that means and receive what's always been there: nature-spirit guidance. It's an antidote to modern disconnection.</p>
<h2>Why Rimrock & Otter</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> Why Rimrock & Otter</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> The disconnect and its antidote.</p>
<p><b>The feeling.</b> The state of the world has left many of us navigating an existence that feels disconnected, empty, and powerless. Maybe there's a longing you can't name, or you're searching for your spark.</p>
<p><b>The reason.</b> Modern society dimmed the part of us that noticed and understood signs from nature spirits, separating us from something critical to a purposeful, profound life and a thriving planet.</p>
<p><b>The answer.</b> Restoring your oneness with nature connects you to the life force in everything — animals, plants, minerals, elements, landforms, even weather. This connection strengthens your perception of your greater place in the world, reigniting your vitality, sense of belonging, and feelings of aliveness.</p>
<h2>Three truths</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> At the core of it all</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Three truths.</p>
<p><b>Nothing is random.</b> Everything and every being in the natural world is relational and reveals wisdom. Nothing is coincidental; it's synchronicity, meaningful serendipity. An eagle flies overhead just as you're contemplating a big change, numbers repeat, or things keep happening in patterns — all signs.</p>
<p><b>We are stardust.</b> It's astrophysics and chemistry. Like the oak, the otter, and the ocean, every atom in our bodies was forged billions of years ago when stars made and spread oxygen, carbon, hydrogen, and nitrogen. We're family with nature, made of the same stuff. We are interconnected wildkind, never separate.</p>
<p><b>It is reachable.</b> We're all born with a keen intuition and a kinship with nature, attuned to its wisdom. Maybe the logistics of life have had you on autopilot, but the path back to deep connectedness with spirits in nature is open to everyone — no special gift, no gatekeepers. Enchantment is yours to experience.</p>
<h2>What we offer</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> What we offer</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> A map back to the enchantment you were born with.</p>
<p>We help you return to honoring the intersection of science and spirit — and all it makes possible. This kind of homecoming strengthens your intuition and the spark of your own spirit. And that matters to the planet and to every being and element sharing it.</p>
<h2>An open door (waitlist)</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> An open door</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> We're creating ways forward.</p>
<p>Virtual group sessions, a podcast, a card deck — all to begin.</p>
<p>If something has you leaning in, please leave your name. We'll reach out as soon as something new is launched.</p>
<p><i>Form note:</i> No pressure. Unsubscribe whenever you'd like.</p>
<h2>Neuroscientist band</h2>
<p><b>Statement:</b> The interconnection of science and spirit.</p>
<p><i>Button: True story</i></p>
<p>It's a connectivity that enables wholeness.</p>
<p>Rimrock & Otter co-founder Kristy Sweetland was a keynote speaker at a recent conference for neuroscientists and neuro-transformational coaches. She wasn't sure how building internal animism would go with a logic-driven crowd of about 75. Animism is the belief that everything in the natural world has a spirit, soul, or consciousness of its own.</p>
<p>During her tutorial on connecting with the spirit of a stone, she looked up to find tears on many of their faces — they described feeling overcome by a sense of "coming home."</p>
<p>One renowned neuroscientist remarked during his own keynote: The world needs more of what Kristy brings — the work of empathy and connection.</p>
<h2>Story wall teaser</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> Signs</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Stories of wonder and peak experiences</p>
<p>Throughout your time on earth, nature spirits show up for you; they're allies. When you're tuned in, it's awe-inspiring — whether you have a powerful "peak experience" that changes your life or a subtle moment of wonder.</p>
<p>We help you tune in and become your own interpreter of signs.</p>
<h3>Featured stories</h3>
<p>"The morning after my mother died, a great horned owl I had never seen before stayed on the porch railing for almost an hour. It looked at me. It did not blink. I cried into a coffee cup until it lifted off." — L.M., Vermont (Owl)</p>
<p>"I asked the river what to do about the job. I felt foolish saying it out loud. Then a stick — long, smooth, river-worn — bumped against my shin three times. I took it home. I quit the job two days later. The stick is on my desk." — J.K., Oregon (Water)</p>
<p>"Same coyote, three nights in a row, at the edge of the yard. Not afraid. Not waiting. Just — present. On the third night I sat down in the grass. We looked at each other for a long time. Something in me settled that has not unsettled since." — D.R., New Mexico (Coyote)</p>
<p><i>Button: Read more & share yours</i></p>
<p><b>Footer tagline:</b> Everything has a spirit you were born to know.</p>
<h1>About (about.html)</h1>
<p><b>Meta description:</b> Meet the founders of Rimrock & Otter, an animism practice teaching nature-spirit connection and signs from the natural world.</p>
<h2>Page intro</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> About</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Two people, taking the next right step for wildkind.</p>
<p>Rimrock & Otter was created to help people light a path to their own wholeness through nature literacy and a reconnection to the earth spirits all around them.</p>
<h2>The founders</h2>
<h3>Kristy Sweetland</h3>
<p><i>Co-founder · Nature-spirit ceremonialist · Teaching</i></p>
<p><i>Rooted in New Mexico: Traditional land of the Pueblos, Ute, and Tiwa people.</i></p>
<p>Kristy has been helping people develop their deep connection with nature for nearly two decades. With a bachelor's degree in organizational psychology and a master's degree in transpersonal psychology, she works with individuals via her private practice, Coaching to Come Alive.</p>
<p>Kristy is a credentialed Certified Professional Transformational Coach and a Board-Certified Executive Coach. She holds professional certificates in neuro-transformation and resilience psychology, too.</p>
<p>After a life-changing, spontaneous shamanic initiation (read about it in her award-winning book, Stark Raving Zen: A Memoir of Coming Alive), Kristy studied with multiple shamanic teachers, the most pivotal Alberto Villoldo, who also teaches channeled light energy.</p>
<h3>Shari Vaccaro</h3>
<p><i>Co-founder · Strategy · Communications · Art</i></p>
<p><i>Rooted in Minnesota: Traditional land of the Wahpekute and Ochethi Sakowin people.</i></p>
<p>Shari is an empath and lifelong existential ponderer, raised with reverence for animals and the outdoors.</p>
<p>In every professional and personal setting, she is a trusted thinking partner and a grounding presence people turn to. She spots possibilities everywhere—and cultivates clarity so others can see it too.</p>
<p>With a bachelor's degree in studio art and years of wordsmithing experience, Shari has spent well over a decade strategizing brand communications, copywriting, and crafting experiences that support people's health.</p>
<p>Bringing Rimrock & Otter to life is a significant step in her ongoing search for meaning. Creating the art for our cards released a torrent of artistry in Shari that had been tucked away too long.</p>
<h2>Why the name Rimrock & Otter?</h2>
<p><i>Button: Find out</i></p>
<p><b>Rimrock:</b> The rim, the elevated boundary of a landform, symbolizes the edge between worlds, the place where perspective changes entirely. When erosion carves away the underlying layers, it becomes rimrock — stone guardians that embody the land's vitality and serve as thresholds between the earthly and spiritual realms.</p>
<p><b>Otter:</b> Otter represents deep connection, nurturing, and the flow of pure joy. With their foundational social traits, such as hand-holding and never-ending playful spirits, they teach us the importance of tangible, tactile togetherness. Otters are the masters of presence and teach us what it means to be in sacred community with each other, the earth, and all wildkind.</p>
<p><b>&:</b> The ampersand connects two relational forces, a reminder that everything has a spirit you were born to know.</p>
<h2>Soul sisters</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> Soul sisters</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Other-level connectedness across 30+ years</p>
<p>A shared love of animals brought Kristy and Shari together in their youth; they worked together at an animal hospital in Minnesota for several years.</p>
<p>Connected on a soul level and with unwavering belief in each other, they've navigated decades of individual growth and transformation. And no surprise, each has always felt most like themselves outdoors exploring nature or marveling at a creature — especially together with their spouses.</p>
<p><i>Photo caption:</i> Some decades ago.</p>
<h2>The founding story</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> The founding story</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Why we came together, and why this offering.</p>
<p>Rimrock and Otter was created as ecosystems, environmental protections for endangered species, and public lands were under full attack in the U.S.</p>
<p>Two longtime best friends — with an ancient worldview that everything in nature has a life force — were among millions who marched, called, sent emails, spread awareness, and donated money. Each, separately, had come to a point where they ached to do more but weren't sure what.</p>
<p>They'd talked about the root of the problem, about the disconnection between humans and everything in the natural world that's non-human.</p>
<p>Kristy had been holding sacred space for others for 15+ years and wanted to extend her work in animism. Shari had been part of the broad layoffs in corporate health care; now seen as a push to redirect her focus toward creativity. One day, in April of 2026, while chatting on the phone, they agreed to open a little door to the possibility of doing something together — and bam. The door flew open with plentiful, undeniable signs. Stars aligned for this partnership.</p>
<p>So, an artist and an author came together to create a humble tool to expand minds and challenge worldviews that see nature as expendable.</p>
<h2>Closing image band</h2>
<p><i>Caption:</i> Childhood enchantment.</p>
<p><b>Footer tagline:</b> Everything has a spirit you were born to know.</p>
<h1>Offerings (whats-coming.html)</h1>
<p><b>Browser title:</b> Offerings</p>
<p><b>Meta description:</b> A preview of what we're currently building — what you can look forward to the soonest: online sessions, a podcast, and a card deck.</p>
<h2>Hero</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> What we offer</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> A map back to the enchantment you were born with.</p>
<p>We're actively building experiences and products — ways to deepen your intuition, heighten your awareness of signs, spark your spirit, and help you see yourself as part of nature.</p>
<h2>Offerings — three across</h2>
<p><b>Headline:</b> What you can look forward to:</p>
<p><b>Virtual group sessions</b> — Come together, feel the energy, and discover ways to build a reciprocal relationship with the natural world. Find community with like-spirited humans, while learning what it means to be an earth empath. With spirit and science, you will harness the power of your heart to strengthen life on earth. <i>Status: Coming this fall</i></p>
<p><b>The podcast</b> — Take in consciousness-expanding conversations about the psychology and deeper implications of our connection and disconnection from Mother Earth. Follow along as we explore the concepts of interconnection and earth medicine. We'll be feeling deeply, getting real, and cultivating hope. <i>Status: Coming this winter</i></p>
<p><b>Card deck</b> — Use this tangible tool to see, learn, and establish interconnection. Interacting with this deck will germinate your earth connection and nature literacy until the spirit of the cards becomes alive within you. This aliveness will sprout roots, bloom, and create an exhilarating new way to experience the world. <i>Status: In development</i> <i>(Button: Peek — reveals card art)</i></p>
<h2>Is this channeling?</h2>
<p><b>Statement:</b> Is this channeling?</p>
<p><i>Button: Get clarification</i></p>
<p>Although our co-founder, Kristy Sweetland, is clairvoyant, clairsentient, clairaudient, and claircognizant, she is not here to channel or translate for you. She believes everyone is born with at least one "clair," and her greatest passion is helping others hone and own their intuitive skills.</p>
<p>Rimrock & Otter helps you tune your radar to deepen your relationship with the natural world, including learning to recognize and interpret your own nature-spirit signs and messages.</p>
<h2>Inline waitlist</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> An open door</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Come through.</p>
<p>We're taking time to shape offerings with purpose.</p>
<p>If something has you leaning in, the best thing you can do is leave your name. We'll let you know when an offering is ready. No noise.</p>
<p><i>Form note:</i> Zero pressure. Unsubscribe whenever you'd like.</p>
<p><b>Footer tagline:</b> Everything has a spirit you were born to know.</p>
<h1>Stories (stories.html)</h1>
<p><b>Browser title:</b> Recognition Stories — Rimrock & Otter</p>
<p><b>Meta description:</b> Real stories of nature-spirit signs and peak experiences — from animal encounters to quiet moments of wonder. Read, sit with, and share your own.</p>
<h2>Page intro</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> Signs</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Stories of wonder and peak experiences</p>
<p>Reading accounts of spirit allies showing up for people may spark something in you. Sometimes, a sign is deeply impactful, a "peak experience," and other times, it's a simple reassurance of our connection. We're here for it all to share in the awe.</p>
<p>If you have your own, there is a place for it at the bottom of this page.</p>
<h2>The wall</h2>
<p>"I asked the river what to do about the job. I felt foolish saying it out loud. Then a stick — long, smooth, river-worn — bumped against my shin three times. I took it home. I quit the job two days later. The stick is on my desk." — J.K., Oregon (Water)</p>
<p>"The first time I asked for a sign, I asked for an eagle. I figured it was specific enough to be unmistakable and rare enough to be impossible. Three days later, one circled the parking lot at the grocery store. I sat in the car and laughed and cried at the same time." — A.P., Wisconsin (Eagle)</p>
<p>"When my marriage ended, I started keeping the small flat stones I found on walks. By the end of that year I had a bowl of them on the kitchen table. I didn't know why I was doing it. Now I do. Every one of them held me, a little, on a day I needed holding." — S.M., Connecticut (Stones)</p>
<p>"The junco came to the kitchen window every morning of my father's last winter. After he died, it stopped. I told myself I was being silly. Then, on the one-year mark, it came back. Just for that morning." — R.H., Maine (Junco)</p>
<p>"I had been thinking, for weeks, about whether to leave. The night I decided, the wind came up so hard it took the porch screen door off its hinges and laid it flat on the lawn. The door — the literal door — was off. I was not going to be argued with." — T.W., Tennessee (Wind)</p>
<p>"I had been sober for ninety days when the deer came into the yard with her two fawns. She let me watch them nurse for ten minutes from the kitchen window, and then she looked right at me. I have not had a drink since. That was four years ago." — C.B., Pennsylvania (Deer)</p>
<h2>Add yours</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> Add yours</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Share what you've noticed and felt.</p>
<p>We read each one with care and may add yours to the wall if you let us know it's okay by checking the box. We can only post 2-3 sentences, so if you share more, please include a condensed version (2-3 sentences), or we will edit it before posting.</p>
<p><i>Checkbox:</i> It's okay to post my story, trimming and rephrasing it if necessary.</p>
<p><i>Form note:</i> We'll never share your full name or email.</p>
<p><b>Footer tagline:</b> Everything has a spirit you were born to know.</p>
<h1>Contact (contact.html)</h1>
<p><b>Meta description:</b> Reach Rimrock & Otter — for inquiries, press, collaborations, or simply to be in touch.</p>
<h2>Page intro</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> Contact</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Say hello.</p>
<p>For inquiries, ideas, collaborations, or simply to be in touch, write to us. We read every note.</p>
<h2>Form + direct</h2>
<p><i>Eyebrow:</i> Direct to Shari or Kristy</p>
<p><b>Headline:</b> Send an email.</p>
<p>If you'd rather skip the form, you can reach us here: hello@rimrockandotter.com</p>
<p>For virtual sessions, please use the form so we can route your note. We typically reply within a week, Monday through Friday.</p>
<p><b>Footer tagline:</b> Everything has a spirit you were born to know.</p>
